> from 2030 to 2050
  result [answered+assumed] workspace_code=world-headed region=GRC scenario=PR_CurPol_CP variable=Emissions|CO2 modelName=e3me

## model-researcher: Researcher comparing integrated assessment models
> Compare GCAM and TIAM on CO2 emissions for the world
  result [answered+assumed] workspace_code=world-headed variable=Emissions|CO2 region=World modelName=gcam scenario=PR_CurPol_CP+PR_NDC_CP
> add baseline
  result [answered+assumed] workspace_code=world-headed variable=Emissions|CO2 region=World modelName=gcam scenario=PR_CurPol_CP+PR_NDC_CP+PR_Baseline
> what does harmonised mean?
  answer [answered (rules)] Harmonisation
  "Harmonisation adjusts model results so that they match common historical data in a base year, making results from different models easier to compare. In IAM PAR"
> tell me about TIAM
  answer [answered (rules)] TIAM_Grantham (TIMES Integrated Assessment Model)
  "ETSAP is recalibrating and improving the geographical resolution of the TIAM model. The new version of the model will be available in 2020 and will cover 31 reg"
> who built it?
  answer [answered (rules)] TIAM_Grantham (TIMES Integrated Assessment Model)
  "TIAM_Grantham (TIMES Integrated Assessment Model) is developed by Grantham, E4SMA."
> where can I compare models side by side?
  navigation [answered (rules)] Model Comparison
  "Open this page on IAMPARIS."
> which models cover SDGs like water or health?
  navigation [answered (rules)] SDG Model Coverage Matrix
  "Open this page on IAMPARIS."

## journalist: Science journalist writing about whether the world is on track
